SUMMARY:Second Saturday Explorer Ride
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T130000
DTSTAMP:20260424T031534Z
UID:um3f9rrqc3e43vqnc0mj7nopip@google.com__20260425
SEQUENCE:2
CREATED:20251104T152227Z
DESCRIPTION:Here’s a link to the March second Saturday ride: https://ri
 dewithgps.com/routes/54187228\n\nThe plan is to go from Davis to Hedgerow 
 Farms to see if any of the flower fields are blooming\, ride to the scenic
  west end of Road 29\, stop in Winters for a snack or lunch at Upper Crust
 \, and then head back to Davis.\n\nMore details below. Please let me know 
 if you need additional information.\nThanks\,\n-Anne\, (916) 206-2922\n\nD
 ate: Second Saturday – March 14\, 2026\nStart time: 9:00 a.m.\nStart l
 ocation: Davis: Westlake Shopping Center\, 1260 Lake Blvd.\nDistance: 45 m
 iles\nContact: Anne Huber\; anneh@dcn.org\; 916-206-2922\nServices (Food\
 , water\, bathrooms): in Winters at mile 32\, so you might want to bring a
  snack\nNo need to RSVP\nRain cancellation or postponement: communicated v
 ia the listserv.\nPace: 14 - 17 mph with regroups. The speed is meant to b
 e an indicator of speed on flat terrain with no wind. People can go faster
  if they want as long as they are willing to regroup. There might be some 
 stopping for scenery.\nRoute: https://ridewithgps.com/routes/54187228\n\n
 For general information about the second Saturday ride and bicycling with 
 the Davis Bike Club\, please see: https://davisbikeclub.org/2nd-sat-explo
 rer-ride/\n\nIt includes the following: “Cycling has inherent risks. Any
  cyclist taking part in a DBC ride releases DBC from any liability. Guests
  are welcome to ride with DBC for one ride\; for subsequent rides\, you mu
 st be a member of the Club. By riding with a DBC group ride you acknowledg
 e that you have read and understand this. Helmets are required on all ride
 s"
LAST-MODIFIED:20260420T145539Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Davis Bike Club
END:VEVENT
