BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"UC Davis Library": "https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/movie-and-an-archive-bottle-shock"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ucdavis_library
SUMMARY:Movie and an Archive: “Bottle Shock” and the True Events of th
 e 1976 Judgment of Paris
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T184500
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52696663626145
DESCRIPTION:Grab some popcorn and join us for a special screening of the i
 ndie comedy Bottle Shock\, starring Alan Rickman\, Chris Pine and Bill Pul
 lman\, as we celebrate the 50th anniversary of the Judgment of Paris. The 
 library will also roll out a special display of items from our Food and Wi
 ne Collections that tell the story of the real people behind the 1976 blin
 d tasting that put California wine on the global map\, such as Steven Spur
 rier (played by Rickman). UC Davis also gets several shout-outs in the fil
 m for its wine expertise!\n\n \nElizabeth McQueen\, Assistant Professor of
  Theatre Studies at Florida State University\, will introduce the film. He
 r research analyzes food and taste as performance\, from contemporary perf
 ormance art to large-scale entertainment sites\, through feminist science 
 and technology studies approaches to environmental and cultural frameworks
 . Her writing can be found in Gastronomica\, Global Performance Studies\, 
 and Theatre Journal. Her upcoming book project\, provisionally titled Tast
 es of Performance\, proposes terroir as a lingering analytic for the anxie
 ties and aesthetics of contemporary consumption. She hosts the food studie
 s podcast\, Esculent.\n\n \n\nPlease register if you plan to attend so we 
 can make sure we have enough popcorn to go around. Drop-ins are also welco
 me. Either way\, we invite you to sit back\, relax and enjoy the show!\n\n
  \n\nNote: Film is 1 hour and 50 minutes. Event time includes discussion w
 ith Professor McQueen and time to explore the historical materials from th
 e library's collections.
LOCATION:Shields Library\, 167
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/movie-and-an-archive-bottle-s
 hock
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
